# DOC-system-triad: Documentation triad (DESIGN · PM · SPRINT)

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| **Paper ID** | `DOC-system-triad` |
| **Subject document(s)** | `DESIGN.oot` + monorepo `PM.oot` + monorepo `SPRINT.oot` |
| **Status** | `draft` |
| **Series** | Documentation system (`DOC-*`) |

## 1. Why this document exists

openOODA needs three non-overlapping control surfaces: vision (DESIGN), progress vs vision (PM), and cycle execution (SPRINT). One file cannot hold stable architecture, honest progress, and high-churn sprint work without rotting.

## 2. Problem statement

If vision and status share a file, DESIGN becomes a lying checklist or sprint noise rewrites architecture. If status and sprint share a file, tip/residual truth fights mid-cycle WIP. Agents then optimize the wrong document.

## 3. Related work (university + commercial)

- **Architecture Decision Records (ADRs)** — decisions with context/consequences (Nygard; adr org). https://adr.github.io/
- **AWS ADR best practices.** https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/architecture/master-architecture-decision-records-adrs-best-practices-for-effective-decision-making/
- **Microsoft — Maintain an ADR.** https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/well-architected/architect-role/architecture-decision-record
- **Living documentation** (Martraire) — docs evolve with the system. https://www.infoq.com/articles/book-review-living-documentation/
- **Scrum product backlog vs sprint backlog.** https://scrumguides.org/scrum-guide.html ; https://www.atlassian.com/agile/scrum/backlogs

## 4. Rationale for openOODA

| Doc | Cadence | Question |
|-----|---------|----------|
| DESIGN | Rare | What is OODA for? |
| PM | After landings | How far vs DESIGN? |
| SPRINT | Every depth push | What are we doing this cycle? |

Research series justify claims; these three govern work.

## 5. Limits and failure modes

Triad fails if PM is not updated after landings; if SPRINT redefines architecture; if DESIGN claims ship status. Public site may summarize; monorepo remains authoritative for PM/SPRINT.

## 6. Alternatives considered

Wiki-only, issue-tracker-only, single mega-README, or oral tradition — all fail multi-agent continuity or honesty. Prefer git-versioned markdown with clear roles.

## 7. Reality (honesty)

Adopted monorepo + site (2026-08). PROGRESS/PROJECT stubbed into PM. Enforcement is process, not yet CI tip-matching.

## 8. Open questions

1. CI check that PM tip SHA equals ooda/main?
2. Publish PM on GitHub org root?

## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Site and monorepo agree on triad roles.
- [ ] No fourth live status doc without stub merge.

